    "objective": "Review the test suite against the landmines principles (https://github.com/interfere-inc/landmines: no test doubles that replace real behaviour, no fixed sleeps, no flake masking through retries or raised timeouts) and adopt them in the best fitting way for this node:test + ESLint project: a dependency-free ratchet check (npm run test:landmines) with an exact per-file allowance that may only shrink, wired into the fast, local and prepush validation tiers; fix the confirmed flaky 1 ms deadline test; and document the rules in the testing guide ENG/test-code-eng.md with attribution.",
